{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1463525-ripping-the-shroud","id":1463525,"title":"Ripping the Shroud","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-11T19:51:59-07:00","id":1463525,"title":"Ripping the Shroud","content":"Hi. <br /> <br /> What happens if something or someone rips the shroud in a given place? (using, for example, a Mage The Ascension Spirit 4 effect)<br /> <br /> Could ghosts go through freely?<br /> Would they be material or would they remain immaterial on the side of the living?<br /> Could they bring relics?<br /> <br /> (Im more interested on the mechanical side than on any metaplot related consequence, really)<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-11T23:55:13-07:00","id":1463546,"title":"","content":"There's a relevant Arcanos art to look at here, the Outrage level 5 initiate art Anger Enough For Two Worlds from the Wraith 20 core, which temporarily rips the Shroud to shreds. The local Shroud rating drops by the number of successes rolled, and regains one point every turn until back to normal. If the Shroud is reduced below 4, its rating is considered to be 3 for any rolls relying on it until it recovers, and for the duration all wraiths in the area can interact with Skinlands objects as if they were solid, and all relics become visible and tangible to Skinlands denizens. Any supernatural power that normally works on only one side of the Shroud can affect everything in the area, invoking the Fog, drawing the attention of Oblivion, and is immediately visible to every supernatural in the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T14:04:41-07:00","id":1463618,"title":"","content":"The first edition corebook had a section on the Calendar and explained there were times of the year when the Shroud was thinnest. For example, between the dawn of October 31 and dawn of November 1 there could be &quot;cracks&quot; in the Shroud, and these cracks could &quot;suck&quot; wraiths into the Skinlands and trap them until the time has passed. Although it does not go into any detail, the assumption is that while such wraiths are still wraiths that they have complete use of their powers and any relics that were on them.<br /> <br /> Presumably it would be like if the wraith was Embodied for the entire time. Anything an Embodied wraith could do, they should be able to do.<br /> <br /> If someone was able to rip the Shroud, I imagine it would be something similar except that mortals could also cross from the Skinlands into the Shadowlands. This is assuming that the Shadowlands and Skinlands still exist separately even though there is just a barest Shroud between them with plenty of &quot;cracks&quot; where passage is possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T05:43:42-07:00","id":1463699,"title":"","content":"Ghosts are still made of ephemeral plasm, so they wouldn't just become physical matter when entering the skinlands. Whether they would be perceptible or not is another question, and depends a great deal on what you need for the game and what source you are looking to. Orpheus, for instance, would indicate that ghosts and relics would remain imperceptible and intangible but have a significantly easier time interacting with things when they want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}